{"title":"Career Roadmap · Clinical Research Associate (CRA)","role":"Clinical Research Associate (CRA)","summary":"A Clinical Research Associate (CRA) supports the conduct of clinical trials by ensuring that study sites follow the approved protocol, applicable regulations, Good Clinical Practice (GCP), and sponsor requirements.","facts":{"Current degree":"Pharm.D (Doctor of Pharmacy)","Course":"Doctor of Pharmacy"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Clinical Research Associate (CRA) supports the conduct of clinical trials by ensuring that study sites follow the approved protocol, applicable regulations, Good Clinical Practice (GCP), and sponsor requirements."},{"type":"p","text":"For a Pharm.D graduate, this is a strong career pathway because the degree provides substantial exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pharmacology"},{"text":"Pharmacotherapeutics"},{"text":"Clinical pharmacy"},{"text":"Patient care"},{"text":"Drug safety"},{"text":"Clinical research"},{"text":"Medical literature"},{"text":"Case documentation"}]},{"type":"note","label":"A practical point","text":"CRA is not always a direct first job for a fresh graduate. Many candidates enter through roles such as Clinical Trial Assistant, Clinical Research Coordinator, Clinical Data Associate, Pharmacovigilance Associate, or Regulatory/Study Start-Up Associate, then progress into CRA positions."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2028"},{"text":"Clinical pharmacy, pharmacology, research methodology and GCP"}],[{"text":"2028–2030"},{"text":"Clinical-trial operations, site documentation and study coordination"}],[{"text":"2030–2033"},{"text":"CRA / Clinical Research Associate responsibilities"}],[{"text":"2033–2036"},{"text":"Senior CRA / Lead CRA / specialized clinical operations"}],[{"text":"2036–2040"},{"text":